WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:20.196
On a dark winter's day, a little girl sat in a cab with her father.

2
00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:25.470
She stared out the window as the cab drove through foggy London.

3
00:00:25.471 --> 00:00:29.987
Sara Crewe was only seven, but she seemed much older.

4
00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:33.305
She was always dreaming and thinking.

5
00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:38.329
At that moment she was thinking about her long trip from India.

6
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:42.636
She had just arrived in London with her father.

7
00:00:42.637 --> 00:00:50.957
It felt strange to travel from a hot, sunny place and arrive in a cold, dark one.

8
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:54.918
Soon the cab stopped in front of a big brick house.

9
00:00:54.919 --> 00:01:01.889
A brass sign on the front door said: "Miss Minchin's Boarding School for Young Ladies."

10
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.518
"Papa, is this the place?" Sara whispered.

11
00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:11.829
"Yes," he replied. "We have reached it at last."

12
00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.259
Sara's mother had died when Sara was born.

13
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.729
Sara's father was an officer in the British army.

14
00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:24.032
He was very rich and handsome and gave Sara whatever she wanted.

15
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:29.950
Sara had lots of toys and clothes. Servants took care of all her needs.

16
00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:33.238
In India she'd had only one worry.

17
00:01:33.239 --> 00:01:37.224
Her father believed that the climate in India wasn't healthy.

18
00:01:37.225 --> 00:01:40.462
So one day he would send her to school in England.

19
00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:44.002
And now that day had come.

20
00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:48.046
Captain Crewe knocked on the door of the school.

21
00:01:48.047 --> 00:01:53.854
A servant answered and led them inside.

22
00:01:53.855 --> 00:02:00.000
Sara looked around at the ugly sitting room with its heavy wooden furniture.

23
00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:03.490
"I don't like it here, Papa," she said.

24
00:02:03.491 --> 00:02:07.619
"But soldiers probably don't like going into battle either."

25
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:13.408
Captain Crewe laughed. "Oh, Sara, you say such wonderful things.

26
00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:19.657
What will I do without you?" He swept her into his arms for a hug.

27
00:02:19.658 --> 00:02:24.419
A moment later the headmistress, Miss Minchin, entered the room.

28
00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.972
The headmistress had large fishy eyes and a large fishy smile.

29
00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:35.790
Sara thought the woman looked just like her school: tall, dull, ugly.

30
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:40.232
Miss Minchin knew that Captain Crewe was rich.

31
00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:43.452
She tried to please him by praising Sara.

32
00:02:43.453 --> 00:02:48.679
"What a beautiful child!" the headmistress exclaimed.

33
00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:55.191
"But I'm not beautiful!" Sara thought. "Miss Minchin is making that up."

34
00:02:55.192 --> 00:03:00.502
Sara stood quietly near her father while he and the headmistress talked.

35
00:03:00.503 --> 00:03:06.346
Because Sara's father was very rich, Sara would have many nice things at school.

36
00:03:06.347 --> 00:03:11.210
There would be a pretty bedroom and sitting room, and a pony and carriage.

37
00:03:11.211 --> 00:03:13.521
A maid would help her.

38
00:03:13.522 --> 00:03:18.650
"Sara reads too much," Captain Crewe told the headmistress.

39
00:03:18.651 --> 00:03:20.894
"Make sure she goes outside.

40
00:03:20.895 --> 00:03:24.691
She should ride her pony or buy some new dolls."

41
00:03:24.692 --> 00:03:32.542
"Oh, Papa!" said Sara. "I don't need a lot of new dolls. I only need Emily."

42
00:03:32.543 --> 00:03:37.142
"Who's Emily?" asked Miss Minchin.

43
00:03:37.143 --> 00:03:40.989
"Tell her, Sara," Captain Crewe said, smiling.

44
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:47.133
"She's a special doll that Papa is going to buy for me," said Sara.

45
00:03:47.134 --> 00:03:52.567
"She'll be my friend when Papa is in India. I'll talk to her about him."

46
00:03:52.568 --> 00:03:56.515
Miss Minchin's large fishy smile grew wider.

47
00:03:56.516 --> 00:04:01.404
"What an unusual child!" she exclaimed loudly.

48
00:04:01.405 --> 00:04:04.462
"She's such a darling girl!"

49
00:04:04.463 --> 00:04:09.319
"Yes," said Captain Crewe. He pulled Sara close.

50
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.043
"She is truly a darling girl.

51
00:04:12.044 --> 00:04:16.387
Please take very good care of her for me, Miss Minchin."

52
00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:20.799
"Oh, I will," the headmistress promised.

53
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:25.318
Sara stayed with her father at his hotel for several days.

54
00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:33.082
He bought her all kinds of expensive clothes—velvet dresses, fur coats, silk stockings.

55
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:40.753
They searched many toy shops looking for Emily but couldn't find her.

56
00:04:40.754 --> 00:04:46.397
"She has to be a doll who can listen to me, Papa," explained Sara.

57
00:04:46.398 --> 00:04:51.036
"Most dolls don't really seem to hear."

58
00:04:51.037 --> 00:04:56.832
So they looked at big dolls and little ones, at dolls with black eyes and dolls with blue ones.

59
00:04:56.833 --> 00:05:03.587
They looked at dolls with brown curls and golden braids, dolls in all kinds of clothing.

60
00:05:03.588 --> 00:05:07.017
But none of them was quite right.

61
00:05:07.018 --> 00:05:13.211
Then one day Sara spotted a doll with golden-brown hair and an intelligent expression.

62
00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:18.412
"Look, Papa! There's Emily!" she cried.

63
00:05:18.413 --> 00:05:25.069
They went into the shop and bought the doll.

64
00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:29.765
Then they went to a dressmaker to order a grand wardrobe for Emily.

65
00:05:29.766 --> 00:05:33.793
Finally the day came when Captain Crewe had to leave.

66
00:05:33.794 --> 00:05:38.256
He and Sara were very sad.

67
00:05:38.257 --> 00:05:46.013
From her window Sara watched him get into a cab. Emily was by her side.

68
00:05:46.014 --> 00:05:52.033
Miss Minchin sent her sister, Miss Amelia, to check on Sara.

69
00:05:52.034 --> 00:05:56.519
"Why is this door locked?" asked Miss Amelia.

70
00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:03.526
"I want to be alone, please," said Sara softly.

71
00:06:03.527 --> 00:06:08.932
Miss Amelia went downstairs and told Miss Minchin about how Sara was acting.

72
00:06:08.933 --> 00:06:13.420
"I've never seen such an odd child," said Miss Amelia.

73
00:06:13.421 --> 00:06:18.845
"She has locked herself in her room, but she's not making any noise at all."

74
00:06:18.846 --> 00:06:23.130
"She's very spoiled," snapped Miss Minchin.

75
00:06:23.131 --> 00:06:25.953
"I'm surprised she isn't kicking and screaming.

76
00:06:25.954 --> 00:06:29.149
All those new clothes are absolutely ridiculous.

77
00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:36.575
Her father treats her like a little princess!"
